think Opened with ListAgents rather than with a file. One peer stood, grain-65, and the file I meant to touch was the file my own last recommend line had left with them, so I named the edit and asked before writing. No reply arrived; the working tree read clean and git log showed their roster work landed at 1b9723594, so the read was that they had released it. Charter law from REDS %291, applied as written.
think The cold roster refused twice before it answered once, and the first refusal was mine. I wrapped the runner in `timeout 900` while giving the tool a 900s window, so at fifteen minutes exactly the runner was killed mid-pass: no close block, no run_verdict, no run card written, and a 60-line tail that had eaten the head. A truncated roster answers nothing about the tree, so it was relaunched whole, nohup and unwrapped, teeing to session-output/silence-roster-cold.txt where a peer can read it.
think That second pass is the one this lap stands on: guards_run=94, guards_green=88, guards_red=6, tree_at_open equal to tree_at_close, tree_moved=no. An unmoved run is the rarer half of the pair here -- the previous two laps both read tree_moved=yes -- so for once the whole-run binding holds rather than only the per-guard verdicts.
think Six reds, and the useful work was telling mine from other bodies'. rule_twin 39/36 is custody gate %7 and stops. width_check 331/329 the card already assigns elsewhere. pond_policy_launcher and pond_enclosure_door are the Mac Pond rows the card gives to Hush, one of which it already diagnoses to a BSD `xargs -r`. That left geode_libraries and remember_git_nib, both mine, both mechanical.
think geode_libraries: the generated library index read 32 witnesses for construction/ where a fresh render read 33. The count is taken by REFERENCE rather than by filename, and the newest witness naming construction/ is tools/r/reds_pin_capacity_witness.rish, added 20260829-041417. No derived-pages-owed marker stood in .git/, so this was not the rebase debt %337 seated the post-commit hook for; the page had simply drifted and nothing had regenerated it since. One `geode_libraries.rish write` closed it GREEN on metal.
think remember_git_nib: the card advertised git nib 1b97235944, which by then was HEAD's great-grandparent -- past the one amend of lag the rule allows, so the guard read stale rather than honest. The named repair is the next work commit's own pin, never a pin-only follow-up, which is what this lap's commit and single amend do.
think The keystone was the row my own last recommend line had left open. tools/co/comlink_r1_dual_stack_witness.rish has stood off the roster since 20260828 because its leg B reads the loopback interface table and requires both address families, so a red there is an environment fact about the host rather than a finding about Comlink -- an unconditional row would turn one bench's configuration into every body's red lap. The capability field seated at 20260829.163028 is exactly the answer, and the runner's own comment says so: "That note asked for this word and declined to guess at it; this is the guess made and proven."
think So the row is now seated -- guard comlink_r1_dual_stack, tier cadence, capability ipv6 -- and the roster paragraph that declined it is rewritten to say what it now is. The scan reads guards_capability_gated=1, guards_unknown_capability=0, tier_cadence 17 -> 18. No new control case was needed: standing_equipment_control.sh already proves all three capability answers on planted pens, so the contract check existed and this row is the asker finally posing the question.
think Measurement beat memory on the one number the row carries. The elder note said 151s; timed alone on this bench the witness read 105s, GREEN, leg A pure and leg B an interface read. Both readings are two orders above the 2s each of its three pure siblings, which is what cadence answers, and the comment now names 105s with the elder reading kept beside it rather than silently replaced.
obs The rota row was 3 -- Water, care and flow -- from N = git rev-list --count HEAD = 3763, and it was not a repeat of the previous lap's aether, so no hand-advance. The fixed seat paid for itself immediately: "the thin edge turned out to include the host itself ... the edge's honest answer is the probe -- ask the host which dialect it speaks, never assume." That is the capability tier's whole argument, written a chapter before the field existed. The cardinal seat, Gall and Conway fused, reads today's collision class straight: a shared checkout is a shared channel, and %291/%345 are the design copying it.
obs Found while reading the rota and left standing on purpose: the water threshold page summarizes Growing a Language as "dogfood and gate" while the page it summarizes already writes "Live in it as first resident, and gate." The banned word survives in the summary of a page that does not use it. The threshold's basename carries a one-clock stamp, so it is testimony and waits for its own circled molt rather than a sweep from this lap. Named here so the next hand finds it.
obs The card's QA report reads A+ 99 with truth_counted=100, and that grade was honest and blind at the same time. Every cited path resolved; five of the Still-open block's clauses were false -- 24,476 bytes for 7,537, 100B free for 17,039, 8 OPEN for 0, 0 foldable for 1, pin_deadlocked=1 for 0. Truth is half counted and half judged, exactly as the rule says, and the counted half cannot see a stale number. Repaired against reds_pin_capacity_scan.sh rather than against memory.
obs The card sits at 24,432 of 24,576 bytes, 144 free, so every edit this lap made was sized to fit rather than merely written: the capability paragraph's Left sentence became the seating sentence, and the Still-open block was rewritten shorter than the block it replaced.
obs Booked no REDS row. The two reds closed here are the ledger's own ratchet class rather than new defects -- a generated page drifting and a nib aging past its allowance are both what their guards exist to catch, and both closed on a witness on metal in the lap that found them.
